--- ARTIFACT NOTES ---
Surface files (apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/EmptyStateThreshold):
  EmptyStateThreshold.kt      (view: stateful entry + stateless EmptyStateThresholdContent renderer +
                               localized noun/message resolvers + previews; GlassPanel container, TeslaGlyphs
                               Check (status.success) + Info (onSurfaceVariant) icons, PanelTitle/Caption/
                               HelperText typography; polite live-region semantics = web role=status).
  EmptyStateThresholdModel.kt (pure port of the web prop handling: EmptyStateThresholdInput ->
                               projectEmptyStateThreshold -> projection of noun (Custom/Default) + message
                               (Custom/Default carrying threshold+current) + section label + description;
                               PII-safe view.opened diagnostics, SLUG=EmptyStateThreshold).
  Web source (web/src/components/feedback/EmptyStateThreshold.tsx) is a PURE PRESENTATIONAL primitive (only
  hook = useTranslation, no fetch) -> no P1/S8 Source/ViewModel (ScoreBadge/FreshnessIndicator/MetricCard
  precedent). The web spec has no data feed, so no loading/error/stale/offline lifecycle is invented (honesty
  covenant: no scope narrowing, no silent drift). Reproduced branches: noun custom/default, message
  custom/default, description present/absent, action present/absent.

i18n: the web component owns two inline-default keys absent from the P1/S10 catalog:
  emptyState.threshold.defaultItem ("items") and emptyState.threshold.message
  ("Need at least {{threshold}} {{noun}} to show meaningful patterns. You have {{current}} so far.").
  Added to the canonical web/src/i18n/en.json and materialized as translation_emptyState_threshold_defaultItem
  + translation_emptyState_threshold_message (message = "Need at least %1$s %2$s ... %3$s so far.", positional
  per INTERPOLATION-MAPPING.md) in values{,-ar,-he}/strings.xml (ar/he English fallback, per P1/S10 policy).
  This mirrors the ScoreBadge predecessor (commit b13ccfc6e: en.json + 3 strings.xml, no catalog/apple/windows
  churn) -- a hand-add, NOT a full gen-i18n regen, because the repo's generated resources are already drifted
  (11 files) and a full regen would be an out-of-scope rewrite. No new caller of the deprecated useSettings /
  unitConversion helpers (Phase-48): the inputs are unitless counts, so no display-unit conversion is needed.

Color/typography tokens (web -> P1/S9, never a raw hex): CheckCircle2 text-emerald-400 -> TeslaGlyphs.Check
  tinted TeslaTokens.status.success; Info text-muted -> TeslaGlyphs.Info tinted onSurfaceVariant; title
  text-sm font-semibold text-primary -> PanelTitle; description text-xs text-secondary -> Caption; message
  text-xs text-muted -> HelperText; container rounded-2xl border bg-surface-1/40 -> GlassPanel (Md padding).

Unit tests (run by the gate, :android:testReleaseUnitTest): EmptyStateThresholdModelTest=8,
  EmptyStateThresholdDiagnosticsTest=3 -> 11 tests, 0 failures, 0 skipped. Cover the noun resolution
  (custom/default), the message resolution (custom override vs default carrying threshold+current distinctly),
  the section-label + description pass-through, the complete default-path projection, and the PII-safe
  view.opened diagnostic (slug only, no count payload).

UI test (src/androidTest/.../emptystatethreshold/EmptyStateThresholdUiTest.kt): per-state localized render
  (title, composed count message with custom noun + with fallback "items", custom-message override hiding the
  default, description, action slot), the polite live-region a11y assertion (web role=status), and the
  one-shot view.opened. It passes ktlintAndroidTestSourceSetCheck and is COMPILE-CLEAN: re-running
  :android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin attributes ZERO errors to EmptyStateThresholdUiTest.kt. The
